    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `customerCode` assignment (`<LAST3>-<NNNN>`) on owner creation, keeping structural impact low by adding a new small function class rather than growing any existing one.\n\n**Behaviour added (new file, WMC_other = 0):**\n- `rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java` \u2014 a single-method step: `NNNN = current owner count + 1`, `LAST3 = first 3 letters of lastName upper-cased`, formatted `%s-%04d`. It mutates the built `Owner` in place (`@Val`) before saving, using `OwnerRepository.findAll().size()` so no repository interface change was needed.\n\n**Wiring:**\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `assignCustomerCode` step between `build` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n**Persistence / serialization (mechanical, no logic changes):**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added the `customerCode` field plus a plain getter/setter (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`). MapStruct auto-maps it into the DTO the same way `initials` is mapped, so no mapper edit was required.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it in `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `customer_code` column (mirroring `registration_date`).\n- `db/hsqldb/data.sql` \u2014 appended a `NULL` to the 10 positional seed owner inserts to match the new column (the other DBs use column-list inserts, so they were unaffected).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` (SMI-/JON- prefixes and the +1 global sequence) and the full suite are green.",
